  "description": "This page includes an overview of the fall course and a list of all the badges needed to earn the course certificate.",
  "image": "public/8404176-CLick here for Overview.png",
  "html": "<p><b>Welcome to the Cultivating Literacy Routines Online Modules, </b>designed to support teachers participating in their first year of the Missouri's Literacy th@t Works professional learning opportunity. ​</p><a data-type=\"image-ref\" data-width=\"60.11904761904761\" class=\"self-center w-full\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/c88db9ba-bb39-4c1a-9612-fc8c1398137d/image-1652125727-22-23_SMLC_Secondary_participate-bundle-purple-475-2x.png\" class=\"w-full\"></a><p>Each year of the Literacy th@t Works program combines in-person meetings with flexible online modules that support teachers in deepening their understanding of literacy practices. Across fall and spring, teachers complete four modules per semester, including a “teacher as researcher” module where they apply new strategies in their classrooms, gather evidence, and share insights with peers and facilitators.</p><p>The online space is designed to help teachers deepen their understanding of routine literacy practices while also receiving targeted support from an online course facilitator, who will help you consider the implications for your specific students and teaching context.</p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-fall-modules-overview\">📋 Fall Modules Overview</h2><p>During the fall online course modules, we will build on your experiences at the Literacy th@t Works Summer Launch and Fall Regroup meetings, and explore a variety of ways to help you integrate Routine Literacy practices into your teaching context. Each module is designed to involve approximately 1-2 hours of self-paced coursework. The course is organized in this way to support your planning for completing the fall modules between now and the end of December.</p><p>You have access to all of the fall modules, so feel free to work at a pace that works best for you and your schedule!</p><p></p><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\" id=\"h_cultivating-literacy-routines-modules\">Cultivating Literacy Routines Modules</h3><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"be8a00e2-04f5-420e-8059-b5ad69a03905\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/be8a00e2-04f5-420e-8059-b5ad69a03905\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Everyday Sparks: Inspiring Writing Ideas</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Everyday writing practices—like notebooks, quicklists, and sprints—ignite creativity and strengthen literacy routines.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/98b9ab3-MOdule%20%231.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"051f2803-9e5c-4ee1-a509-49457dab93b8\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/051f2803-9e5c-4ee1-a509-49457dab93b8\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Reading to Write: They Say / I Say</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">The They Say / I Say framework helps students enter conversations with texts—listening, responding, and developing their own voices as writers.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/d434527-MOdule%202.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"6672cfe1-cef9-44b3-b82f-11b3bf4af905\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/6672cfe1-cef9-44b3-b82f-11b3bf4af905\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Reading to Write: Say-Mean-Matter</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">With Say-Mean-Matter, students learn to see beyond summary and consider the meaning and significance of what they read.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/5c5584d-MOdule%203.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"a3215d34-bf38-4692-9b42-be53f7de2a66\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/a3215d34-bf38-4692-9b42-be53f7de2a66\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Teacher as Researcher: Try, Reflect, Share</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Teacher-research is about curiosity—asking what’s happening with students and what it might mean.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/aa7503e-MOdule%204.png\"></div></a></div><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-earn-recognition\">🏅 Earn Recognition</h2><p>As you work through the modules, you can earn digital credentials to recognize your progress and learning. For each module, you’ll automatically receive a <b>badge</b> when you participate in the discussion, where you’ll reflect on your learning and exchange ideas with other teachers. You also have the opportunity to earn a <b>microcredential</b> by submitting coursework for the module; your facilitator will review your work, provide individual feedback, and award the microcredential. Once you’ve earned all badges and microcredentials for the fall modules, you’ll automatically receive the <b>Cultivating Literacy Routines credential</b>, marking your full completion of the semester’s work.</p><div data-type=\"badge-embed\" data-badge-id=\"072b926b-40d4-4cca-b7e4-8f9459cc9aec\" data-badge-type=\"credential\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/badge/072b926b-40d4-4cca-b7e4-8f9459cc9aec\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Credential</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Cultivating Literacy Routines</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This credential recognizes your full participation in the Literacy th@t Works fall online course modules. By completing all modules, earning each badge and microcredential, and engaging in reflection and discussion, you have demonstrated a sustained commitment to building literacy routines and practicing teacher inquiry. This credential signifies your accomplishment in completing the fall semester coursework and your readiness to carry these practices forward into your classroom and future professional learning.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/e846af2-Credential%20Cultivating%20Literacy.png\"></div></a></div><p></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-let-s-get-started\">➡️ Let's get started!</h2><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"be8a00e2-04f5-420e-8059-b5ad69a03905\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/be8a00e2-04f5-420e-8059-b5ad69a03905\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Everyday Sparks: Inspiring Writing Ideas</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Everyday writing practices—like notebooks, quicklists, and sprints—ignite creativity and strengthen literacy routines.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/98b9ab3-MOdule%20%231.png\"></div></a></div><p></p>",
